Z||000000||stevemasleid||05-20-2001||06:35 PM||||Thanks to “haze_performance” for telling me about this GREAT site. I met that dude at an illegal drag racing spot on the south side of Chicago at around 2 A.M. Friday night.<BR>Anyway…I tried to pull my steering column, but to my dismay, I couldn’t remove the actual steering linkage from the car. I removed the bolt from the clamp that is located just above the universal joint. I then gave the steering wheel a big yank. Oops…About six or seven inches of steering shaft came out of the hole that is found behind my brake pedal. <BR>Did I break something?<BR>How do I put the shaft back into the hole?<BR>Did I undo the wrong bolt to remove my busted column?<BR>Is the correct bolt inside the cockpit or under the car?<BR>Ogre mentioned something about the shift interlock…. Can I keep the old switch assembly it’s connected to intact and avoid breaking the interlock?<BR>Ogre also said to remove a bolt from the U-Joint? What does he mean?<BR>I have digital pictures of my steering column that I can email if you cannot visualize any of these descriptions. <BR>THANK YOU FOR YOUR HELP!!!<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||stevemasleid||05-21-2001||01:16 AM||||how do I put a .jpg on this post?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||05-21-2001||01:35 AM||||The bolt that you should have removed is at the lower end of the column by the brake pedal. (sounds like you got the right one) I don't have any idea why it came apart the way it did unles the lower end was worn out, or is telescoped, I don't know that it is or isn't as I haven't had one apart on the bottom.<P>The shift interlock is for automatics and yes you can save the old one intact if you so desire.<P>To post pics, click the box at the bottom of the page that says 'Pennock's Image Poster' to download the stuff you need.<BR>||||reg||1
